{"tool_name":"nonlinear-drift-correction-spm-orthogonal-image-pairs","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"nonlinear-drift-correction-spm-orthogonal-image-pairs","home":"https://www.mathworks.com/matlabcentral/fileexchange/51941-nonlinear-drift-correction-from-scanning-probe-microscopy-spm-orthogonal-image-pairs","summary":"Correct nonlinear drift distortions in scanning probe images.","addition_date":"2021-05-05T11:09:12Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-24T20:21:32.670255Z","tool_type":["Library"],"version":["1.1.0.0"],"collections":["File Exchange","MATLAB"],"accessibility":"Open access (with restrictions)","biotools_curie":"biotools:nonlinear-drift-correction-spm-orthogonal-image-pairs","cost":"Free of charge (with restrictions)","credit":[{"name":"Colin Ophus","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"],"url":"https://www.mathworks.com/matlabcentral/profile/6173252-colin-ophus"}],"edit_permission":{"authors":["wangmengjun"],"type":"group"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Image analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3443"},{"term":"Microscope image visualisation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3552"}]}],"name":"Nonlinear Drift Correction from Scanning Probe Microscopy (SPM) Orthogonal Image Pairs","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"Kigaard","publication":[{"doi":"10.1016/j.ultramic.2015.12.002","metadata":{"abstract":"Unwanted motion of the probe with respect to the sample is a ubiquitous problem in scanning probe and scanning transmission electron microscopies, causing both linear and nonlinear artifacts in experimental images. We have designed a procedure to correct these artifacts by using orthogonal scan pairs to align each measurement line-by-line along the slow scan direction, by fitting contrast variation along the lines. We demonstrate the accuracy of our algorithm on both synthetic and experimental data and provide an implementation of our method.","authors":[{"n